# Project Name

One line about what the project does.

## Commands

- Install: `npm install`
- Run in dev: `npm run dev`
- Tests (all): `npm test`
- Single test: `npm test -- path/to/file`
- Lint/format: `npm run lint`
- Typecheck: `npm run typecheck`

## Architecture (only what isn't obvious)

- `src/api/`: HTTP handlers, no business logic
- `src/domain/`: business rules, no I/O
- `src/infra/`: database, queues, external clients

## Conventions

- Strict TypeScript; avoid `any`
- Commits follow Conventional Commits
- Tests live next to the code: `foo.ts` → `foo.test.ts`

## Watch out

- Never edit `src/generated/` by hand; it is generated by `npm run codegen`
- Don't commit `.env`; use `.env.example`
- Database migrations: always create them with `npm run db:migrate:new`

